            <ArticleTitle>Copper-mediated phospha-annulation to attain water-soluble polycyclic luminophores.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10954-10957</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06882d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 6-membered P-heterocycle has been fused with a polyaromatic framework through intramolecular transformation of anthracene-based phosphine induced by CuCl2. The resulting water soluble phosphonium fluorophores exhibit extremely high quantum efficiency along with prominent stability and low toxicity that make them suitable for one- and two-photon imaging purposes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
